 "summary": "The post-PR surface is minimal and canonical: no compatibility artifacts, no exposed bodies (`(rfl)` projection lemmas, no `@[expose]`), and `pairing`/`moment` carry a complete characteristic API (`*_def`, both congr lemmas, `pairing_pow`, `moment_natCast_add_one`, `pairing_eq_plusFunctional`, the `mellinDis` bridge, and smul-homogeneity). The simp set \u2014 field lemmas, `pairing_smul`/`moment_smul`, and the N = 1, 2 values \u2014 neither loops nor misfires, and general infrastructure (`integral_poly_mul_rpow`, the PlusFunctional and harmonic-number additions) is public in its own home rather than hidden as private.",
